15:03.790 --> 15:05.380
My name is Elizabeth.

15:07.130 --> 15:11.930
Now, our club is going global{moving toward the world}!

15:11.930 --> 15:14.470
Nice to meet you Eli-chan.

15:14.470 --> 15:16.350
The pleasure is mine.

15:16.640 --> 15:20.980
Having more members is a good thing,
but we have five members now.

15:20.980 --> 15:22.730
What's the matter?

15:22.730 --> 15:24.440
We have an odd number of members.

15:24.440 --> 15:27.190
Soft tennis is played in doubles.

15:27.190 --> 15:32.700
{When we have a team}In a competition one person will always be left out.

15:32.700 --> 15:36.320
I see, so that's it.

15:36.320 --> 15:39.660
It's a harsh, competitive world anyway. {Its a harsh cometitive world anyway}

15:39.660 --> 15:42.410
{FIBI: WHAT THE-? }Let's get along and train hard{Harth} together. {Well, bear no grudges/hardfeelings against one another and work hard / train dilligently together}

15:42.410 --> 15:45.210
Some things can't be helped though.

15:45.210 --> 15:47.250
Why are you looking at me?!

15:48.130 --> 15:51.510
Anyway, looks like it's your first time playing soft tennis.

15:51.510 --> 15:54.550
I'll give you some pointers, Eli-chan.{I'll go give some pointers to Eli-chan.}

15:54.550 --> 15:56.510
As the senior{sempai}! As the club head!{club head in preview for ep3 as well - cc}

15:56.760 --> 15:58.520
If you will.

15:58.520 --> 16:00.520
Leave it to me!

16:11.360 --> 16:14.030
Using the methods from hard tennis won't work.{Hard tennis playing methods}

16:15.000 --> 16:26.920
<b>Hard Tennis</b>

16:15.280 --> 16:20.120
In hard tennis the rebound is strong and travels farther.

16:18.590 --> 16:26.920
<b>Soft Tennis</b>

16:20.120 --> 16:25.920
In soft tennis the ball is soft, with a weak rebound and shorter range.

16:25.920 --> 16:32.710
That means that in hard tennis, to keep the ball
from flying{reflecting} too far, one has to use weak spins.

16:26.890 --> 16:32.640
<b>Hard Tennis</b>

16:32.640 --> 16:37.050
<b>Soft Tennis</b>

16:32.710 --> 16:36.840
You merely have to receive the ball and hit it back.

16:36.840 --> 16:37.970
I see.

16:37.760 --> 16:43.140
<b>Trying _
her best...</b>

16:37.970 --> 16:40.430
It looks a little different.

16:40.430 --> 16:43.140
Just grasp the feeling of it first.

16:43.140 --> 16:44.850
<b>An hour later...</b>

16:48.770 --> 16:55.780
<b>I taught 
her a little 
too well...</b>

16:49.570 --> 16:52.900
This child learns too fast...

16:52.900 --> 16:55.780
Just an hour of practicing and she already surpasses you?

16:57.410 --> 16:59.620
What are you doing?

17:00.330 --> 17:06.000
When Eli-chan gives a backhand,
she holds the racket in a really weird way{posture}.

17:06.000 --> 17:12.260
<b>Fore</b>

17:06.330 --> 17:10.210
Ah, it's different from hard tennis.

17:07.210 --> 17:12.260
<b>Back</b>

17:10.210 --> 17:12.260
Backhands and forehands use the same side.

17:14.420 --> 17:16.380
Using the same side as a forehand...

17:16.380 --> 17:19.100
Using the same side as a forehand...

17:19.100 --> 17:22.640
Using the same side as a... forehand!

17:25.640 --> 17:27.270
What a cool stance.

17:27.310 --> 17:28.190
<b>Seems like she's
correct afterall...</b>

17:28.560 --> 17:30.570
Okay. You're all practicing.

17:30.820 --> 17:33.110
